// Applied live 2026-11-27 about 22:07 on Adam's yes (docs/evidence/second-check-2026-11-27). Lets jorah-guard's second check (plugins/jorah-guard/lib/second.js) call
// Sonnet through api.runtime.llm.complete. OpenClaw refuses a plugin that picks its own model
// unless the plugin's entry trusts it; without this every check fails closed with
// LLM_COMPLETION_NOT_AUTHORIZED and Adam sees the card as before.
//
// Measured on jorah-dev, 2026-11-27, with exactly these two keys on a probe plugin: a brief that
// matched Adam's words passed in 2-5 s, a brief for other work failed with the right reason, and
// the call ran on the claude-cli runtime (Max plan). Naming the target agent was refused even with
// these keys, so the guard names none (allowAgentIdOverride stays off).
//
// Dry run on the PC:
//   openclaw --profile jorah config patch --file /opt/jorah/config/pc/second-check-llm.patch.json5 --dry-run
// Expected: "Dry run successful" with updates under plugins.entries.jorah-guard.llm only.
// Undo: { plugins: { entries: { "jorah-guard": { llm: null } } } }
{
  plugins: {
    entries: {
      "jorah-guard": {
        llm: {
          allowModelOverride: true,
          allowedModels: ["anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5"],
        },
      },
    },
  },
}
